   "reply": "The tests pass (2 of 2). Run this from the project root (`<run>\\work\\L1\\b\\w`) in bash:\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n```\n\n- **Why not pytest:** `python -m pytest` fails because pytest isn't installed. The tests are written with `unittest`, so you don't need it.\n- **Why `PYTHONPATH=src`:** the package lives in `src/ledgerlite`, and the tests do `from ledgerlite import Ledger`. Without it the import fails.\n- **PowerShell or cmd:** `PYTHONPATH=src` as a prefix is bash syntax. In PowerShell, run `$env:PYTHONPATH=\"src\"; python -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.\n\nI didn't change any files.",
