   "reply": "I added `Ledger.close(name)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`. It raises `ValueError` if the account's balance isn't zero. Otherwise it removes the account. A name that doesn't exist raises `KeyError`, the same as `balance()` does.\n\nI also added `test_close_requires_zero_balance` in `tests/test_ledger.py`. It checks that closing a funded account fails and leaves the account in place. It then checks that closing succeeds once the balance is back to zero.\n\nThe full suite passes: 3 tests, all OK. I ran it with `PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests`.",
